# Cloudflare Pages headers — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# Security headers on every response
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Revalidate HTML so a new deploy shows immediately (no stale edge copy)
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ── CSS and JS: DECLARED, not inherited ─────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 2026-08-04. Until today these two classes had no rule here at all, and
# that was not a decision — it was a gap the Cloudflare zone happened to be
# filling. `nikatru.com`'s Browser Cache TTL was 14400, and Cloudflare
# edge-caches .css and .js by extension, so anything of those types this zone
# served was stamped `max-age=14400` whatever the origin declared. The override
# is now off (the zone is on "Respect Existing Headers"), which fixed a real
# bug on subly.nikatru.com — /flutter_bootstrap.js and /main.dart.js were being
# given a four-hour browser cache against a declared `max-age=0`, so a
# returning visitor ran the PREVIOUS build and reported its version honestly,
# invisible to exactly the force-update kill switch that exists for it. Turning
# it off also left .css and .js here with nothing choosing a policy at all.
#
# MEASURED, not assumed, 2026-08-04:
#   · this site serves NO external CSS or JS today. Every page carries its
#     styles in an inline <style> block, and /assets/tokens.css and
#     /assets/base.css both return 404. (Those files live in
#     sites/_shared/assets/ — the Eleventy layer whose `_site/` output is
#     gitignored and deploys nowhere; see sites/_shared/README.md.)
#   · a path with NO rule here gets the Cloudflare Pages default, which
#     measured as `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` — robots.txt,
#     sitemap.xml and llms.txt all returned it.
#
# So the two rules below change nothing that is served today. THAT IS THE
# POINT: a policy file has to declare the class BEFORE the first file of that
# class exists, because the alternative is that the first stylesheet ships on
# whatever the platform or the zone happens to be defaulting to that week.
#
# WHY REVALIDATE AND NOT `immutable`. The CSS these sites will serve once they
# migrate onto sites/_shared is `tokens.css` and `base.css` — STABLE names with
# CHANGING content. `tokens.css` is GENERATED by Style Dictionary out of
# packages/tokens (it changed today) and `base.css` is hand-edited; neither
# name moves when its bytes do. `immutable` on a stable name means a CSS fix
# never reaches anyone who has already visited — for a year, and without even a
# revalidation on an explicit reload. This takes the same one-round-trip
# bargain apps/subly/web/_headers takes for its entry points.
#
# Declared at ANY DEPTH (`/*.css`, not `/assets/*.css`) on purpose: the gap
# being closed is a file arriving somewhere nobody wrote a rule for, and a
# directory-scoped rule reopens it the moment a stylesheet lands at the root.
#
# ⚠️ NOT the Pages Function. /api/subscribe is served by
# functions/api/subscribe.js as a ROUTE, not as a .js asset, so neither rule
# below touches it.
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Long-cache immutable static assets.
# ⚠️ RECORDED GAP — this is not a claim that these are content-addressed.
# `founder-v4.jpg` / `founder-v4.webp` carry their version IN THE NAME, which
# is what makes `immutable` correct for them. `icon-16/32/192/512.png`,
# `apple-touch-icon.png` and `og-image.png` do NOT: replacing the brand mark
# under one of those names would not reach a returning visitor for a year.
# Left as-is DELIBERATELY — these are the page's heaviest bytes and re-cutting
# them is a brand decision, so the call is the owner's. Nothing here has gone
# quiet about it: assert-web-cache-policy.mjs prints the stable-named
# `immutable` paths on every run rather than failing the build, so the gap
# cannot become permanent by being invisible.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/site.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
